CORE
main.cpp
--cpp20
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ const T & parameter: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ two template parameters: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
The parser skipped a lambda's template-parameter-list, and the type checker
treated a lambda as generic only when a parameter's type was `auto' or a
bare name, so `const T &' left T unknown.  libc++'s __synth_three_way
(std::tuple's operator<=>, views::take) has this shape.
